+/// How many days ahead the search looks before it answers "never".
+///
+/// Five years, and the number is chosen rather than picked: the rarest thing a five-field expression
+/// can name is 29 February, which comes round every fourth year, so a schedule that matches nothing
+/// in five years can never match at all. That is what makes `None` an answer instead of a search
+/// that does not come back — `0 0 31 2 *` is legal to write and names nothing for ever.
+const HORIZON_DAYS: i64 = 366 * 5;
+
